  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 206 AM MDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nEarly morning radar shows showers with a few embedded lightning \nstrikes working through central and extreme southeast Idaho as \nfeatured in CAMs. Southwest flow will continue to lift monsoonal \nmoisture into Southeast Idaho and support daily shower and \nthunderstorm chances through mid to late week. Shower and \nthunderstorm coverage will trend more scattered today with activity \ncontinuing to lift northward and primarily being focused across the \ncentral mountains and east/southeast highlands throughout the day \nand afternoon. Today's high temperatures will run several degrees \ncooler than yesterday's. A shortwave on Wednesday will result in \nboth increased convective activity and a noticeable cool down with \ntemperatures returning to around normal to slightly below normal \nwith widespread 80s across the low elevations. Storms will be \ncapable of locally heavy rainfall with outflow winds the strongest \ntoday at 40 to 50 mph and closer to 35 to 45 mph on Wednesday.\nDry conditions and above normal temperatures return late week.",
